{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9744c87805561aac","type":"tool_result","content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n\n<head><script>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>  <title>[2608.11755v1] MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques</title>\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"180x180\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/apple-touch-icon.png\">\n  <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/favicon-32x32.png\">\n  <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"16x16\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/favicon-16x16.png\">\n  <link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/site.webmanifest\">\n  <link rel=\"mask-icon\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/safari-pinned-tab.svg\" color=\"#5bbad5\">\n  <meta name=\"msapplication-TileColor\" content=\"#da532c\">\n  <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#ffffff\">\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/css/arXiv.css?v=20260318\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"print\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/css/arXiv-print.css?v=20200611\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/css/browse_search.css\" />\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/arxiv-header-footer.css?v=20260626\" />\n  <script language=\"javascript\" src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/accordion.js\" ></script>\n  <script language=\"javascript\" src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/optin-modal.js?v=20250819\"></script>\n  \n  <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11755\"/>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Abstract page for arXiv paper 2608.11755v1: MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques\"><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"arXiv.org\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11755v1\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/arxiv-logo-fb.png\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image:secure_url\" content=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/arxiv-logo-fb.png\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"700\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"arXiv logo\"/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Long-form song generation models continue to improve in duration, structural integrity, and acoustic complexity, making reliable aesthetic rewards increasingly important for aligning these models with human preferences. However, reward models for complete songs remain limited, and existing evaluators typically predict scores in a single forward pass without providing readable explanations. We introduce MUSECRITIC, a semi-scalar reward model that generates a natural-language critique covering five aesthetic dimensions and uses it as an intermediate representation to predict continuous reward scores. MUSECRITIC follows a two-stage training pipeline: a teacher model first provides high-quality critiques for supervised fine-tuning, after which the fine-tuned model generates its own critiques for reward learning, mitigating distribution shift between training and inference. On an in-domain test set of 200 SongEval songs, MUSECRITIC reduces macro-averaged mean squared error from 0.2875 to 0.2316 and improves macro-averaged LCC, SRCC, and Kendall&#39;s tau to 0.9068, 0.8838, and 0.7178, respectively. On the out-of-domain Music Arena benchmark with 733 preference pairs, it achieves the highest accuracy of 71.35%. Moreover, using MUSECRITIC with GRPO improves Muse-0.6B on all nine aesthetic metrics from SongEval and Audiobox Aesthetics. These results demonstrate that critique-conditioned reward modeling reduces scoring error and provides an effective optimization signal for song generation. The project repository is available at https://github.com/WuqnEl/MuseCritic.\"/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@arxiv\"/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\"/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through...\"/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Long-form song generation models continue to improve in duration, structural integrity, and acoustic complexity, making reliable aesthetic rewards increasingly important for aligning these models...\"/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://static.arxiv.org/icons/twitter/arxiv-logo-twitter-square.png\"/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:image:alt\" content=\"arXiv logo\"/>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" media=\"screen\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/css/tooltip.css\"/><link rel=\"stylesheet\" media=\"screen\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"https://static.arxiv.org/js/bibex-dev/bibex.css?20200709\"/>  <script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/mathjaxToggle.min.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script>  <script src=\"//code.jquery.com/jquery-latest.min.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script>\n  <script src=\"//cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/js-cookie@2/src/js.cookie.min.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script>\n  <script src=\"//cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/dompurify@2.3.5/dist/purify.min.js\"></script>\n  <script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/toggle-labs.js?20241022\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script>\n  <script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/cite.js\" type=\"text/javascript\"></script><meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zhuang, Jiabao\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Jiang, Changhao\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wang, Hanchen\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Chen, Jiahao\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Yang, Zhixiong\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Xiang, Zhenghao\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Cao, Yifei\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Sun, Jiajun\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Li, Hui\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zhang, Ming\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Ji, Tao\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Gui, Tao\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Zhang, Qi\" /><meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Huang, Xuanjing\" /><meta name=\"citation_date\" content=\"2026/08/12\" /><meta name=\"citation_online_date\" content=\"2026/08/12\" /><meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.11755\" /><meta name=\"citation_arxiv_id\" content=\"2608.11755\" /><meta name=\"citation_abstract\" content=\"Long-form song generation models continue to improve in duration, structural integrity, and acoustic complexity, making reliable aesthetic rewards increasingly important for aligning these models with human preferences. However, reward models for complete songs remain limited, and existing evaluators typically predict scores in a single forward pass without providing readable explanations. We introduce MUSECRITIC, a semi-scalar reward model that generates a natural-language critique covering five aesthetic dimensions and uses it as an intermediate representation to predict continuous reward scores. MUSECRITIC follows a two-stage training pipeline: a teacher model first provides high-quality critiques for supervised fine-tuning, after which the fine-tuned model generates its own critiques for reward learning, mitigating distribution shift between training and inference. On an in-domain test set of 200 SongEval songs, MUSECRITIC reduces macro-averaged mean squared error from 0.2875 to 0.2316 and improves macro-averaged LCC, SRCC, and Kendall&#39;s tau to 0.9068, 0.8838, and 0.7178, respectively. On the out-of-domain Music Arena benchmark with 733 preference pairs, it achieves the highest accuracy of 71.35%. Moreover, using MUSECRITIC with GRPO improves Muse-0.6B on all nine aesthetic metrics from SongEval and Audiobox Aesthetics. These results demonstrate that critique-conditioned reward modeling reduces scoring error and provides an effective optimization signal for song generation. The project repository is available at https://github.com/WuqnEl/MuseCritic.\" />\n</head>\n\n<body ><div class=\"flex-wrap-footer\">\n    <a href=\"#content\" class=\"ds-skip-link\">Skip to main content</a>\n  \n  \n  \n<header class=\"ds-site-header\">\n  <a aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/IgnoreMe\" class=\"is-sr-only\"></a>\n\n  <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/\" class=\"ds-site-header-logo\" aria-label=\"archive home\">\n    <img src=\"/static/base/1.0.1/images/arxiv-logo-primary-light.svg\" alt=\"archive\">\n  </a>\n\n  <button type=\"button\" id=\"ds-nav-toggle\" class=\"ds-site-header-nav-toggle\"\n    aria-label=\"Open menu\" aria-controls=\"ds-site-header-nav\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\">\n      <line x1=\"3\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"6\"/>\n      <line x1=\"3\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"12\"/>\n      <line x1=\"3\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"18\"/>\n    </svg>\n  </button>\n\n  <nav class=\"ds-site-header-nav\" id=\"ds-site-header-nav\" aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a id=\"arxiv-search-toggle\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/search\"\n      aria-controls=\"arxiv-search-overlay\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n      <svg class=\"ds-nav-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\">\n        <circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"8\"/>\n        <line x1=\"21\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"16.65\" y2=\"16.65\"/>\n      </svg>\n      Search\n    </a>\n    <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/user/create\">Submit</a>\n    <a href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/about/donate.html\">Donate</a>\n    <span class=\"ds-site-header-divider\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n      <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/login\" class=\"ds-site-header-login\">Log in</a>\n  </nav>\n</header>\n\n<div class=\"arxiv-search-overlay\" id=\"arxiv-search-overlay\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"arxiv-search-panel\" role=\"search\">\n    <form method=\"GET\" action=\"https://arxiv.org/search\">\n      <label for=\"arxiv-search-input\" class=\"is-sr-only\">Search arXiv</label>\n      <input type=\"text\" name=\"query\" id=\"arxiv-search-input\" autocomplete=\"off\"\n        placeholder=\"Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...\">\n      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"searchtype\" value=\"all\">\n      <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"source\" value=\"header\">\n    </form>\n    <div class=\"arxiv-search-hint\">\n      Press Enter to search &middot; <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/advanced\">Advanced search</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n    <main>\n      <div id=\"content\">\n<!--\nrdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"\n         xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\"\n         xmlns:trackback=\"http://madskills.com/public/xml/rss/module/trackback/\">\n    <rdf:Description\n        rdf:about=\"/abs/2608.11755\"\n        dc:identifier=\"/abs/2608.11755\"\n        dc:title=\"MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques\"\n        trackback:ping=\"/trackback/2608.11755\" />\n    </rdf:RDF>\n--><div id=\"abs-outer\">\n\n  <div class=\"leftcolumn\">\n    <div class=\"subheader\">\n      <h1>Computer Science > Sound</h1>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"header-breadcrumbs-mobile\">\n      <strong>arXiv:2608.11755v1</strong> (cs)\n    </div>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n<div id=\"content-inner\">\n  <div id=\"abs\">\n    <div class=\"dateline\">\n  [Submitted on 12 Aug 2026]</div>\n    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques</h1>\n    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhuang,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiabao Zhuang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Jiang,+C\" rel=\"nofollow\">Changhao Jiang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Wang,+H\" rel=\"nofollow\">Hanchen Wang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Chen,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiahao Chen</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yang,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zhixiong Yang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Xiang,+Z\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zhenghao Xiang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Cao,+Y\" rel=\"nofollow\">Yifei Cao</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Sun,+J\" rel=\"nofollow\">Jiajun Sun</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Li,+H\" rel=\"nofollow\">Hui Li</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+M\" rel=\"nofollow\">Ming Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ji,+T\" rel=\"nofollow\">Tao Ji</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Gui,+T\" rel=\"nofollow\">Tao Gui</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Zhang,+Q\" rel=\"nofollow\">Qi Zhang</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Huang,+X\" rel=\"nofollow\">Xuanjing Huang</a></div>            <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques, by Jiabao Zhuang and 13 other authors</div>\n    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"/pdf/2608.11755v1\">View PDF</a>\n    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.11755v1\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n\n\n\n    <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n            <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>Long-form song generation models continue to improve in duration, structural integrity, and acoustic complexity, making reliable aesthetic rewards increasingly important for aligning these models with human preferences. However, reward models for complete songs remain limited, and existing evaluators typically predict scores in a single forward pass without providing readable explanations. We introduce MUSECRITIC, a semi-scalar reward model that generates a natural-language critique covering five aesthetic dimensions and uses it as an intermediate representation to predict continuous reward scores. MUSECRITIC follows a two-stage training pipeline: a teacher model first provides high-quality critiques for supervised fine-tuning, after which the fine-tuned model generates its own critiques for reward learning, mitigating distribution shift between training and inference. On an in-domain test set of 200 SongEval songs, MUSECRITIC reduces macro-averaged mean squared error from 0.2875 to 0.2316 and improves macro-averaged LCC, SRCC, and Kendall&#39;s tau to 0.9068, 0.8838, and 0.7178, respectively. On the out-of-domain Music Arena benchmark with 733 preference pairs, it achieves the highest accuracy of 71.35%. Moreover, using MUSECRITIC with GRPO improves Muse-0.6B on all nine aesthetic metrics from SongEval and Audiobox Aesthetics. These results demonstrate that critique-conditioned reward modeling reduces scoring error and provides an effective optimization signal for song generation. The project repository is available at <a href=\"https://github.com/WuqnEl/MuseCritic\" rel=\"external noopener nofollow\" class=\"link-external link-https\">this https URL</a>.\n    </blockquote>\n\n    <!--CONTEXT-->\n    <div class=\"metatable\">\n      <table summary=\"Additional metadata\"><tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\">\n            <span class=\"primary-subject\">Sound (cs.SD)</span>; Computation and Language (cs.CL)</td>\n        </tr><tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11755\">arXiv:2608.11755</a> [cs.SD]</span></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\">\n              <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11755v1\">arXiv:2608.11755v1</a> [cs.SD]</span> for this version)\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\">              <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.11755\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2608.11755</a><div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n              <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n                <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h12v-64h-12c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h64c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v100h12c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v24z\" class=\"\"></path></svg>\n                <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Focus to learn more</span>\n              </button>\n              <!-- tooltip description -->\n              <div role=\"tooltip\" id=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n                <span class=\"left-corner\"></span>                  arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)</div>\n            </div>\n          </td>\n        </tr></table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n    <div class=\"submission-history\">\n      <h2>Submission history</h2> From: Jiabao Zhuang [<a href=\"/show-email/9789a5c0/2608.11755\" rel=\"nofollow\">view email</a>]      <br/>    <strong>[v1]</strong>\n        Wed, 12 Aug 2026 07:49:17 UTC (614 KB)<br/>\n</div>\n  </div>\n  <!--end leftcolumn-->\n<div class=\"extra-services\">    <div class=\"full-text\">\n      <a name=\"other\"></a>\n      <span class=\"descriptor\">Full-text links:</span>\n      <h2>Access Paper:</h2>\n      <ul>\n  <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>\nView a PDF of the paper titled MuseCritic: Learning Multi-Aspect Song Rewards through Natural-Language Aesthetic Critiques, by Jiabao Zhuang and 13 other authors</div><li><a href=\"/pdf/2608.11755v1\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li><li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2608.11755v1\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li><li><a href=\"/src/2608.11755v1\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source\n </a></li></ul>\n      <div class=\"abs-license\"><a href=\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\">view license</a></div>\n    </div>\n    <!--end full-text-->    <div class=\"browse\">\n    <h3 class=\"browse-context-heading\">Current browse context:</h3>\n  <div class=\"current\">cs.SD</div>\n\n  <div class=\"prevnext\">\n<span class=\"arrow\">\n      <a class=\"abs-button prev-url\" href=